/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuojCheng/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuojCheng/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuojCheng/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuojCheng/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuojCheng/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuojCheng/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"jobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Hypercomputer/maxtext/actions/runs/32999133815/jobs","logs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Hypercomputer/maxtext/actions/runs/32999133815/logs","check_suite_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Hypercomputer/maxtext/check-suites/89396151681","artifacts_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Hypercomputer/maxtext/actions/runs/32999133815/artifacts","cancel_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Hypercomputer/maxtext/actions/runs/32999133815/cancel","rerun_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Hypercomputer/maxtext/actions/runs/32999133815/rerun","previous_attempt_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Hypercomputer/maxtext/actions/runs/32999133815/attempts/2","workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Hypercomputer/maxtext/actions/workflows/297948505","head_commit":{"id":"bc209fb6b7363be8d45287da70163883c64224d9","tree_id":"60a5e86261bda97e343b010e65e71209903616f9","message":"Add explicit sharding support for the Qwen3 model family\n\nOnboards the `qwen3`, `qwen3_moe` and `qwen3_custom_moe` decoder blocks to\n`shard_mode=explicit`, following the pattern already used for `llama2` and\n`deepseek`.\n\nModel changes:\n- `AttentionWithNorm` (shared by the dense, MoE and custom-MoE Qwen3 layers)\n  now builds `out_sharding` / `mlp_intermediate_sharding` from the logical axis\n  rules, passes `shard_mode` into its RMSNorms, and threads `out_sharding`\n  through the norms, attention and MLP/MoE calls. Without this the attention\n  out-projection has no legal output layout to infer under explicit axes.\n- `nn.with_logical_constraint` is replaced with `maybe_shard_with_logical`, so\n  the same call site reshards under explicit axes and constrains under auto.\n\nNormalization fix:\n- The RMSNorm scale is stored with the `norm` logical axis (-> `tensor`), which\n  is right for a norm over the embedding axis but wrong for a per-head QK norm:\n  its `head_dim` axis is unsharded while the neighbouring `heads` axis is the\n  one on `tensor`, so the multiply put `tensor` on two axes of the result and\n  JAX rejected it under tensor parallelism. The scale is now aligned with the\n  activation's last-dim sharding before the multiply. This only runs under\n  `ShardMode.EXPLICIT` and is a no-op when the two already agree.\n\nConfig:\n- `use_multimodal` is now rejected with explicit sharding; the Qwen3 vision and\n  audio encoders are not onboarded (a reshape in the patch embed fails).\n- `qwen3_next` and `qwen3_5` remain unsupported (gated-delta-net attention).\n\nTests:\n- `train_tests.py` gains an auto-vs-explicit parity test covering all three\n  decoder blocks, each with the parallelism that stresses it most, plus a\n  ZeRO-1 + gradient-accumulation parity test for the dense and MoE decoders\n  that exercises the reduced/unreduced gradient PartitionSpec labels.\n- `pyconfig_test.py` covers the config guards.\n\nVerified on a v6e-4: all configurations match the auto-sharding baseline.\nThe qwen3-0.6b golden input-sharding dump gains two entries because the\ndecoder now reports its activation shardings via `maybe_shard_with_logical`.","timestamp":"2026-08-26T18:20:05Z","author":{"name":"NuojCheng","email":"chengnuojin@google.com"},"committer":{"name":"NuojCheng","email":"chengnuojin@google.com"}},"repository":{"id":607845880,"node_id":"R_kgDOJDr9-A","name":"maxtext","full_name":"AI-Hypercomputer/maxtext","private":false,"owner":{"login":"AI-Hypercomputer","id":181000646,"node_id":"O_kgDOCsnZxg","avatar_ur